{"id":131,"date":"2020-09-21T18:03:48","date_gmt":"2020-09-21T18:03:48","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?page_id=131"},"modified":"2022-08-23T17:37:20","modified_gmt":"2022-08-23T17:37:20","slug":"alumni-wall","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/alumni-wall\/","title":{"rendered":"Alumni Wall"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim-30 has-background-dim has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left pad-5\" style=\"background-color:#161228;min-height:600px\"><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-1964\" alt=\"\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-scaled.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-scaled.jpg 2560w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/alumni-spotlight-background-photo-1-16x12.jpg 16w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n<h1>Alumni Wall<\/h1>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\">\n<p>To implement its vision, AIMS targets the brightest young African students, shaping them as independent thinkers and problem-solvers capable of innovating and propelling the continent\u2019s economic prosperity. Africa\u2019s youth are at the heart of the AIMS innovation and transformation ecosystem, which consists of a set of academic and non-academic programs expertly tailored to provide AIMS learners with a unique post-graduate training experience on the continent.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This rich network of highly skilled and learned individuals will be interconnected to help support one another as well as benefit from employment and advanced educational opportunities from AIMS. On a whole, this alumni body will build a legacy and carry out our vision of transforming Africa, ensuring that our goal as an organization is met.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Meet a<\/strong> <strong>few of our alumni, still growing, still evolving and hoping to make a lasting impact within STEM!<\/strong><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\">\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5-no-top\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\">\n<div class=\"row w-00\">        \n\n\t<div class=\"col-md-4 col-lg-3 \"> <a class=\"profile-card-link\" href=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student\/fadekemi-janet-osaye\/?studenbio\"> \n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"profile-card-img img-bg\" style=\"background-image:url('https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/osaye_fadekemi.jpg')\">\n\n\n\n\n\n <\/div>\n<div class=\"profile-card-bottom pad-5 bg-primary center-text\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-name white-text center-text sans-serif-bold\"><p> <strong> Dr. Fadekemi Janet Osaye <\/strong><\/p><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"profile-card-name sans-serif-light white-text center-text\">Assistant Professor of Mathematics &#8211; Alabama State University<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n<\/a> \n<\/div>\n\n\n\n\n        \n\n\t<div class=\"col-md-4 col-lg-3 \"> <a class=\"profile-card-link\" href=\"https:\/\/aims.e